      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start and the tone is perfect for the library. \n\nHowever, I just checked the report from the technical team, and the temporal indexer is performing much worse than we expected on this batch. It's flagging almost all of these summaries as \"low density\" because they don't have enough specific date stamps in the DD/MM/YYYY format. If the density score is too low, these documents won't show up in the digital search tool at all, which basically makes the work useless for researchers.\n\nCan you try a second version? I really mean it when I say I don't want a list of dates, but we absolutely need to hit a higher density of specific DD/MM/YYYY formatted dates so the indexer actually picks them up. Try to weave them into the narrative more effectively if you can, but we need to see those specific date patterns to make the indexer happy.",
